15:26.120 --> 15:28.120
The first thing you need to know
about bio fuels

15:28.120 --> 15:32.120
is that when internal combustion
engines were being developed,

15:32.120 --> 15:34.120
two types of engines were
designed.

15:34.120 --> 15:38.120
Engines that ran off highly
refined oils, gasoline type
engines,

15:38.120 --> 15:42.120
and engines that ran off of
basically just purified oil,

15:42.120 --> 15:44.120
or slightly refined oil.

15:44.120 --> 15:46.120
And that was a diesel type
engine.

15:46.120 --> 15:49.120
An important thing to also note
is that both of those engines

15:49.120 --> 15:52.120
were originally developed to use
either gasoline

15:52.120 --> 15:55.120
or purified oils from both
petroleum oil

15:55.120 --> 15:57.120
and vegetable oil sources.

15:57.120 --> 16:01.120
Now diesel type engines can run
off either purified oil,
vegetable oil,

16:01.120 --> 16:04.120
or petroleum oil, or a slightly
distilled version of that oil

16:04.120 --> 16:06.120
called diesel.

16:06.120 --> 16:10.120
Bio diesel is diesel fuel that
is derived from vegetable oil
sources

16:10.120 --> 16:12.120
or animal fat sources.

16:12.120 --> 16:16.120
Modern petroleum diesel engines
could run on straight vegetable
oil

16:16.120 --> 16:19.120
but the engine wouldn't last
very long.

16:19.120 --> 16:21.120
They make it work and not ruin
the engine

16:21.120 --> 16:23.120
requires a conversion kit.

16:23.120 --> 16:25.120
Not counting homemade kits,

16:25.120 --> 16:28.120
the only professional conversion
process available

16:28.120 --> 16:31.120
for a modern petroleum diesel
engine to convert

16:31.120 --> 16:35.120
to straight vegetable oil
replaces the injectors

16:35.120 --> 16:38.120
as heaters to the tank and
replaces other components
necessary

16:38.120 --> 16:42.120
to run the diesel engine on
straight vegetable oil.

16:42.120 --> 16:46.120
These professional conversions
can also run on pure biodiesel

16:47.120 --> 16:51.120
any bio diesel blend or on
straight dirty or petroleum
diesel.

16:51.120 --> 16:54.120
A professional conversion of
this type is the only conversion

16:54.120 --> 16:58.120
that could be called a true bio
fuel or bio diesel conversion.

16:58.120 --> 17:02.120
